## What this delivers

The live Adversary correctly refused a seal whose evidence was non-probative: the Court re-ran the
command in a sandbox **without the change**, so only vacuous self-contained commands (`echo`) could
pass. B2.N runs the command in a workspace **with the change applied**, so evidence that actually
imports and exercises the change passes iff the change is real — and fails for its negation. Verified
out-of-band: the sandboxed venv-python imports the package and runs a behaviour assertion in the
workspace (exit 0 when the target exists, exit 1 when absent).

## Evaluation Checklist

